  ('zcrm_1579374000000173868', 'John Kach', 'In-Active', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'Adela Carvajal', 'Christina', 'Carvajal', 'zcrm_1579374000000150037', 'John Kach', 'bowxtie_@hotmail.com', NULL, '305 877 5222', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2015-08-11 16:26:56', '2025-08-08 14:51:39', 'Christina Carvajal', '510 NE 62nd Street', 'miami', 'FL', '33138', FALSE, NULL, NULL, 'USD', 1.0, '2025-08-08 14:51:39', NULL, 'n/a', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<b>3/01/2014 09:50 PM</b>: <b>3/1/2014 04:25 PM</b>: JK Spoke to Christina at 10:30.... said she''s be available at 4.... called no answer, left foicemail...<hr><b>2/24/2014 07:26 PM</b>: JK - Rescheduled for Tuesday at 6<hr><b>2/20/2014 04:43 PM</b>: Aetna Classic 5000 Monthly premium  $85/mo One enrollee Premium before tax credit $250/mo Deductible $150/yr Per individual Out-of-pocket Maximum $1,175/yr Per individual Copayments/Coinsurance: Primary Doctor: $5 Specialist Doctor: $15 Generic Prescription: 4 ER Visit: $100   myCigna Health Flex 2750 Monthly premium $115/mo One enrollee Premium before tax credit $280/mo Deductible  $200/yr Per individual Out-of-pocket Maximum $575/yr Per individual Copayments/Coinsurance: Primary Doctor: $30 Specialist Doctor: $60 Generic Prescription: 4 ER Visit: 20% Coinsurance after deductible<hr><hr />', 'Aetna', 'Aetna - Classic 5000 Silver', NULL, '0.0', 'To Be Determined', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Import', NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 'Contacts_2026_03_20.csv'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000000173869', 'John Kach', 'Enrolled - 2019', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'Mary Francois', 'Phyllis', 'Johnson', 'zcrm_1579374000000150037', 'John Kach', 'phyl@noemail.com', NULL, '786 506 1245', NULL, NULL, '1955-08-03', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'zcrm_1579374000000086007', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2015-08-11 16:26:56', '2025-08-08 14:51:39', 'Phyllis Johnson', '16401 NW 22nd court', 'Mami', 'FL', '33054', FALSE, NULL, NULL, 'USD', 1.0, '2025-08-08 14:51:39', NULL, 'N/A', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<b>3/01/2014 09:50 PM</b>: <b>2/28/2014 09:49 PM</b>:  Silver $10 Copay HMO Carelink HMO Health Maintenance Organization: A type of health insurance plan that usually limits coverage to care from doctors who work for or contract with the HMO. It generally won''t cover out-of-network care except in an emergency. An HMO may require you to live or work in its service area to be eligible for coverage. HMOs often provide integrated care and focus on prevention and wellness. | Silver Plans are put into 5 categories. These 5 categories (catastrophic, bronze, silver, gold, and platinum) are based on how you and the plan expect to share the costs for health care. Silver plans cover 70% of the total average cost of care. The category you choose affects how much your premium costs each month and what portion of the bill you pay for things like hospital visits or prescription drugs. It also affects your total out-of-pocket costs - the total amount you''ll spend for the year if you need lots of care. CoventryOne Monthly premium   $22/mo One enrollee Premium before tax credit $537/mo Deductible The amount you owe for health care services your health insurance or plan covers before your health insurance or plan begins to pay. For example, if your deductible is $1,000, your plan won''t pay anything until you%u2019ve met your $1,000 deductible for covered health care services subject to the deductible. The deductible may not apply to all services. $0/yr  Per individual Out-of-pocket Maximum Your expenses for medical care that aren''t reimbursed by insurance. Out-of-pocket costs include deductibles, coinsurance, and copayments for covered services plus all costs for services that aren''t covered. $1,500/yr  Per individual Copayments/Coinsurance: A copay is a fixed amount (for example, $15) you pay for a covered health care service, usually when you get the service. The amount can vary by the type of covered health care service. Coinsurance is your share of the costs of a covered health care service, calculated as a percent (for example, 20%) of the allowed amount for the service. You pay coinsurance plus any deductibles you owe. For example, if the health insurance or plan%u2019s allowed amount for an office visit is $100 and you''ve met your deductible, your coinsurance payment of 20% would be $20. The health insurance or plan pays the rest of the allowed amount. Primary Doctor: No Charge Specialist Doctor: $25 Generic Prescription: $5 ER Visit: $100<hr><b>2/28/2014 09:24 PM</b>: Health plans for one individual, age 58 , living in Miami-Dade County, FL.  Based on a household size of one and income of $12,500, you may qualify for a $515/month tax credit you can choose to apply to your premium for these plans. This tax credit has been applied to the premiums below.  You may also qualify for the reduced out-of-pocket expenses shown in the plans below. <hr><hr />', 'Coventry', 'Coventry Silver $10 HMO Carelink', '537', '50.0', 'Health Insurance', NULL, '2014-04-01', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'false', NULL, NULL, '12', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '6', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Import', NULL, 'false', 'false'