ed from the EPO to the Bison Silver PPO. <br /><HR><br /><B>3/25/2014 09:47 PM</B>: WS- Call CO Health Op to see if have her info. C4HCO can''t tell if the life change event has been submitted to CO Health Op yet. <br /><HR><br /><B>3/17/2014 06:53 PM</B>: WS- Super happy that I just saved her an immense amount of stress and time. Psyched to have CO Health Op PPO Bison Silver Plan. Asked her to call me on March 26th to follow up to find out status of our request for changes. <br /><HR><br /><B>3/17/2014 05:56 PM</B>: Incident # 140 317-002 542 to update change of event and change of plan. Worst case she will have a cost of $126.70 and best case cost of $57.85, $500 max out of pocket, $300 deductible. Has been submitted. Call back asap if we need to change it at all. <br /><HR><br /><B>3/17/2014 05:27 PM</B>: WS- Showing Suzy can get about a $301 subsidy and change to CO Health Op Silver PPO. Her cost will be $126.70. Calling her in a moment to complete her change of event form over the phone. <br /><HR><br /><B>3/16/2014 04:31 PM</B>: Makes $40K now and gets $36 subsidy. Lives with domestic partner/male but they file their taxes separately. <br /><HR><br /><B>2/19/2014 05:04 PM</B>: She will be leaving job and starting own biz in 1-2 months. Will qualify for a subsidy at that time and then wants to change plan with life changing event option or do so before March 31st deadline. Perfers to have an HMO or PPO, not an EPO. She had a RMHP before but was going to cost $400+ up from $178. <br /><HR><br /><B>2/19/2014 05:02 PM</B>: Signed up already for CO Health Op Bison EPO but realizing it''s super limited for doctors and wants to change. Hadn''t made 1st pmt but was going to when got off phone for Feb. coverage (if they allow pmt for Feb. part way through the month). Paying $355.42 mo. <br /><HR><br /><br /><HR><hr />', 'Bright Health', 'CO Health Op Bison Silver PPO', '981.47', NULL, 'Health Insurance', 'Member and Spouse', '2014-04-01', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'fa